# Mobile Web Game Development Guidelines

## Overview
This document outlines best practices and guidelines for developing a touch-based Metroidvania game for mobile web platforms, focusing on responsive touch controls, efficient rendering, and progressive enhancement.

## Core Principles
- **Performance First**: Optimize for mobile devices with varying capabilities
- **Touch-Optimized**: Design all interactions around natural touch gestures
- **Progressive Enhancement**: Start with basic functionality, enhance as abilities are unlocked
- **Cross-Browser Compatibility**: Ensure consistent experience across all modern mobile browsers

## Touch Input Implementation

### Gesture System
- Implement a unified gesture system with these core interactions:
  - **Tap**: Simple press and release for basic actions
  - **Swipe**: Direction-based movement with velocity detection
  - **Hold and Release**: Charging mechanism with visual feedback

### Input Processing Guidelines
```javascript
// Recommended pattern for touch input handling
function setupTouchControls(canvas) {
  let touchStartTime = 0;
  let touchStartPos = { x: 0, y: 0 };
  let isHolding = false;
  let chargeLevel = 0;
  
  canvas.addEventListener('touchstart', (e) => {
    e.preventDefault(); // Prevent scrolling
    touchStartTime = performance.now();
    touchStartPos = { 
      x: e.touches[0].clientX, 
      y: e.touches[0].clientY 
    };
    isHolding = true;
    
    // Start visual charging feedback
    startChargeAnimation();
  });
  
  canvas.addEventListener('touchmove', (e) => {
    if (!isHolding) return;
    
    const currentPos = { 
      x: e.touches[0].clientX, 
      y: e.touches[0].clientY 
    };
    
    // Update charging direction indicator
    updateChargeDirection(touchStartPos, currentPos);
  });
  
  canvas.addEventListener('touchend', (e) => {
    const touchEndTime = performance.now();
    const touchDuration = touchEndTime - touchStartTime;
    
    if (touchDuration < 200) {
      // Short touch = Tap action
      performTapAction(touchStartPos);
    } else if (isHolding) {
      // Release after hold = Charged action
      performChargedAction(chargeLevel, touchStartPos, lastTouchPos);
    }
    
    isHolding = false;
    chargeLevel = 0;
    stopChargeAnimation();
  });
}
```

### Visual Feedback
- Provide immediate visual feedback for all touch interactions
- Use subtle animations to confirm input registration
- Implement directional indicators for charged actions
- Consider haptic feedback where supported (use navigator.vibrate API)

## Rendering Optimization

### Canvas Performance
- Use requestAnimationFrame for smooth animation
- Implement proper game loop with fixed update steps
- Utilize offscreen canvas for complex rendering operations
- Layer multiple canvases for performance (background, character, UI layers)

### Asset Management
- Implement sprite atlases to reduce draw calls
- Use progressive loading of assets based on game progress
- Preload assets for upcoming areas during gameplay
- Compress textures appropriately for mobile devices

## Ability System Integration

### Ability Unlock Structure
- Design a modular ability system that enhances existing gesture controls
- Store player progression in localStorage or IndexedDB
- Implement ability requirements as prerequisites for accessing new areas
- Use event-driven architecture to handle ability activation

### Ability Enhancement Pattern
```javascript
// Example of gesture enhancement through abilities
class GestureController {
  constructor(player, world) {
    this.player = player;
    this.world = world;
    this.abilities = {
      dash: false,
      doubleJump: false,
      wallClimb: false,
      chargedAttack: false
    };
  }
  
  unlockAbility(abilityName) {
    if (this.abilities.hasOwnProperty(abilityName)) {
      this.abilities[abilityName] = true;
      // Trigger any visual effects or tutorials
      this.world.showAbilityUnlockEffect(abilityName);
    }
  }
  
  handleSwipe(direction, force) {
    if (this.abilities.dash) {
      return this.player.performDash(direction, force);
    } else {
      return this.player.move(direction, force * 0.5);
    }
  }
  
  handleHoldRelease(direction, chargeLevel) {
    if (this.abilities.chargedAttack && chargeLevel > 0.8) {
      return this.player.performChargedAttack(direction);
    } else if (this.abilities.doubleJump) {
      return this.player.jump(direction, chargeLevel);
    } else {
      return this.player.basicAction(direction);
    }
  }
}
```

## Progressive Web App Features

### Offline Support
- Implement service workers for asset caching
- Store game state in browser storage
- Provide clear indication of offline mode
- Handle reconnection gracefully

### Installation Experience
- Create a web manifest for "Add to Home Screen" functionality
- Design appropriate app icons for various platforms
- Optimize startup performance after installation
- Implement proper splash screen

## Performance Monitoring

### Key Metrics
- Target 60fps rendering on mid-range devices
- Monitor and optimize touch input latency (<50ms response)
- Track memory usage, especially for texture assets
- Implement debugging tools for performance monitoring

### Testing Guidelines
- Test on actual devices, not just emulators
- Implement automated performance tests
- Validate touch controls across different screen sizes
- Test under varying network conditions

## Accessibility Considerations
- Provide alternative control schemes
- Support high contrast mode
- Include options for gesture sensitivity
- Allow customization of visual feedback intensity

